D("poltroonery",{etymology:E("From poltroon + -ery; poltroon came through French from Italian poltrone ‘coward, idler’, while -ery forms a noun for conduct or a quality. The deeper origin of poltroon is uncertain.",null,"poltrone (deeper origin uncertain)","-ery","Etymonline, poltroon (https://www.etymonline.com/word/poltroon)."),contexts:[C("poltroonery.s1","文學","The captain condemned the officer’s poltroonery after he abandoned the crew during the storm.","暴風雨中那名軍官拋下船員，船長譴責他的怯懦行徑。","Poltroonery is contemptible lack of courage.","Poltroonery is the object of condemned; after gives the cowardly act.","The officer leaves others in danger instead of facing the crisis.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The rescue crew showed poltroonery by entering the flood to save trapped families despite personal danger.","The rescue crew showed courage by entering the flood to save trapped families.","Poltroonery is contemptible cowardice; taking a risk to rescue others shows courage.")],quiz:[Q("poltroonery.q1","poltroonery.s1","meaning","Poltroonery is ___.",["shameful cowardice","careful technical skill","generous hospitality"],"shameful cowardice","The noun means a contemptible lack of courage.","meaning"),Q("poltroonery.q2","poltroonery.s1","context","Which action shows poltroonery?",["Abandoning companions in danger to avoid any personal risk","Helping evacuate people during a fire","Admitting a mistake in public"],"Abandoning companions in danger to avoid any personal risk","Deserting others from fear is cowardly conduct.","context"),Q("poltroonery.q3","poltroonery.s1","word-choice","The critic called the general’s retreat ____ rather than a wise strategy.",["poltroonery","pollution","polyphony"],"poltroonery","The critic describes the retreat as contemptibly cowardly.","word-choice"),Q("poltroonery.q4","poltroonery.s1","meaning","Why is poltroonery a harsh judgment?",["It condemns a person’s lack of courage.","It praises a person’s kindness.","It names an area of flat land."],"It condemns a person’s lack of courage.","The word is strongly critical of cowardly behavior.","meaning")]});
D("polyandrous",{etymology:E("From Greek polyandros ‘having many husbands’, from polys ‘many’ + anēr/andros ‘man’; -ous forms an adjective for a mating or marriage system in which a female has multiple male partners.","poly","andros","-ous","Etymonline, polyandry (https://www.etymonline.com/word/polyandry)."),contexts:[C("polyandrous.s1","社會","The anthropologist documented a polyandrous marriage in which one woman had two husbands.","人類學家記錄了一種一妻多夫婚姻，其中一名女性有兩位丈夫。","Polyandrous describes a mating or marriage system in which a female has more than one male partner.","Polyandrous modifies marriage; in which specifies the arrangement.","One woman has two husbands, matching the term’s definition.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The report called a marriage polyandrous because one man had several wives and no woman had multiple husbands.","The report called the marriage polygynous because one man had several wives; polyandrous means one woman has multiple husbands.","Polyandry specifically involves a woman with more than one husband; the described arrangement is polygyny.")],quiz:[Q("polyandrous.q1","polyandrous.s1","meaning","A polyandrous marriage involves ___.",["one woman with more than one husband","one man with several wives","two people who are not married"],"one woman with more than one husband","The word refers to a female with multiple male partners.","meaning"),Q("polyandrous.q2","polyandrous.s1","context","Which field note describes a polyandrous arrangement?",["A woman has two husbands in the same marriage system.","A man has three wives.","Two siblings share a home."],"A woman has two husbands in the same marriage system.","This matches the definition of polyandry.","context"),Q("polyandrous.q3","polyandrous.s1","word-choice","The researcher compared a ____ society with neighboring marriage systems.",["polyandrous","pompous","polygonal"],"polyandrous","The adjective describes the marriage arrangement being studied.","word-choice"),Q("polyandrous.q4","polyandrous.s1","word-formation","The Greek element andros in polyandrous refers to ___.",["a man or husband","a many-sided shape","a color"],"a man or husband","Andros is the genitive form related to Greek anēr ‘man’.","word-formation")]});
D("polychrome",{etymology:E("From French polychrome and Greek polychrōmos ‘many-colored’, from poly- ‘many’ + chrōma ‘color’; it describes multicolored decoration and can be a work executed in several colors.","poly","chrōma","-e","Etymonline, polychrome (https://www.etymonline.com/word/polychrome)."),contexts:[C("polychrome.s1","藝術","The restorer uncovered polychrome paint beneath the statue’s later coat of white plaster.","修復師在雕像後來塗上的白色石膏下，發現了多色彩繪。","Polychrome means painted or printed in several colors.","Polychrome modifies paint; beneath locates the earlier layer.","The uncovered decoration uses multiple colors rather than one.") ,C("polychrome.s2","藝術","The museum displayed a small polychrome carved horse painted red, blue, and gold.","博物館展出一匹彩繪小木馬，塗有紅、藍和金色。","A polychrome can be a work of art executed in many colors.","Polychrome is the object of displayed; painted lists its colors.","The noun names the multicolored art object itself.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The artist produced a polychrome panel using only unpainted gray stone with no colored sections.","The artist produced a monochrome panel using only unpainted gray stone with no colored sections.","Polychrome requires several colors; a single gray tone is monochrome.")],quiz:[Q("polychrome.q1","polychrome.s1","meaning","A polychrome surface is ___.",["painted in several colors","left entirely colorless","made only of one shade"],"painted in several colors","Poly- means many and chrome relates to color.","meaning"),Q("polychrome.q2","polychrome.s2","context","Which object could be called a polychrome?",["A carved figure painted red, blue, and gold","A plain unpainted stone block","A black-and-white word list"],"A carved figure painted red, blue, and gold","The artwork is executed in multiple colors.","context"),Q("polychrome.q3","polychrome.s1","word-choice","The temple wall has ____ tiles in blue, green, and ochre.",["polychrome","polyandrous","poltroonery"],"polychrome","The tiles are decorated in several colors.","word-choice"),Q("polychrome.q4","polychrome.s2","meaning","What distinguishes a polychrome artwork from a monochrome one?",["It uses multiple colors.","It has no subject.","It is made only of wood."],"It uses multiple colors.","Polychrome refers to a work executed in several colors.","meaning")]});
D("polygamous",{etymology:E("From Greek polygamos ‘married many times or to many’, from polys ‘many’ + gamos ‘marriage’; the adjective describes a person or system involving marriage to more than one person at once.","poly","gamos","-ous","Etymonline, polygamous (https://www.etymonline.com/word/polygamous)."),contexts:[C("polygamous.s1","通用","The documentary compared polygamous households with monogamous ones without assuming every family followed the same customs.","紀錄片比較多配偶家庭與一夫一妻家庭，沒有假定每個家庭都遵循相同習俗。","Polygamous means practicing marriage to more than one person at the same time.","Polygamous modifies households; without introduces a caution about variation.","The term describes the household’s marriage form, not every individual practice.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","A couple married only to each other was described as polygamous, although neither had another spouse.","A couple married only to each other was described as monogamous; polygamous means marriage to more than one person at once.","Polygamous requires multiple spouses at the same time; one exclusive pair is monogamous.")],quiz:[Q("polygamous.q1","polygamous.s1","meaning","A polygamous marriage is one in which ___.",["a person has more than one spouse at the same time","each person has exactly one spouse","the spouses are not married"],"a person has more than one spouse at the same time","The adjective refers to simultaneous marriage to multiple people.","meaning"),Q("polygamous.q2","polygamous.s1","context","Which description fits a polygamous household?",["One spouse has several partners within a marriage system","Two people marry and have no other spouses","A family lives in a polygon-shaped house"],"One spouse has several partners within a marriage system","Multiple spouses are the defining feature.","context"),Q("polygamous.q3","polygamous.s1","word-choice","The historian studied a ____ royal household with several simultaneous spouses.",["polygamous","polychrome","pompous"],"polygamous","The household includes more than one spouse at once.","word-choice"),Q("polygamous.q4","polygamous.s1","meaning","Which situation is not polygamous?",["Two spouses are married only to each other.","One person has multiple spouses at once.","A marriage system allows several concurrent spouses."],"Two spouses are married only to each other.","An exclusive pair has only one spouse per person.","meaning")]});
D("polygamy",{etymology:E("From Greek polygamia, from polys ‘many’ + gamos ‘marriage’; the term covers marriage to more than one person at once, including polygyny and polyandry.","poly","gamos","-y","Etymonline, polygamy (https://www.etymonline.com/word/polygamy)."),contexts:[C("polygamy.s1","社會","The legal historian distinguished polygamy, which permits multiple spouses, from serial marriages that occur one after another.","法律史學家區分允許同時有多位配偶的多偶制，與先後發生的多次婚姻。","Polygamy is marriage to more than one person at once.","Polygamy is the object of distinguished; which clause defines it.","The key contrast is concurrent spouses versus marriages at different times.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The historian defined polygamy as marrying one person after another over many decades, with no overlapping marriages.","The historian defined serial monogamy as successive marriages without overlap; polygamy means multiple spouses at once.","Polygamy involves concurrent spouses, not merely several marriages in sequence.")],quiz:[Q("polygamy.q1","polygamy.s1","meaning","Polygamy means ___.",["marriage to more than one person at the same time","marriage to one person only","living alone without marriage"],"marriage to more than one person at the same time","The term refers to simultaneous multiple spouses.","meaning"),Q("polygamy.q2","polygamy.s1","context","Which arrangement is an example of polygamy?",["A marriage system allows a person multiple spouses concurrently.","A person remarries years after a divorce.","Two people marry once and remain exclusive."],"A marriage system allows a person multiple spouses concurrently.","Concurrent rather than successive spouses define polygamy.","context"),Q("polygamy.q3","polygamy.s1","word-choice","The book examines the history and legal treatment of ____ in several societies.",["polygamy","polyphony","pollution"],"polygamy","The book studies systems of multiple simultaneous marriage.","word-choice"),Q("polygamy.q4","polygamy.s1","meaning","Why is a series of separate marriages not necessarily polygamy?",["The spouses may not overlap in time.","The people may speak several languages.","The marriages may be colorful."],"The spouses may not overlap in time.","Polygamy concerns multiple spouses at once, not successive unions.","meaning")]});
D("polygon",{etymology:E("From Greek polygōnon ‘many-angled’, neuter of polygōnos, from polys ‘many’ + gōnia ‘angle’; a polygon is a closed plane figure bounded by straight line segments.","poly","gōnia","-on","Etymonline, polygon (https://www.etymonline.com/word/polygon)."),contexts:[C("polygon.s1","數學","The surveyor marked a six-sided polygon on the map to show the parcel’s boundary.","測量員在地圖上標出一個六邊形，以表示地塊邊界。","A polygon is a closed plane shape bounded by straight lines.","Polygon is the object of marked; on the map gives its location.","The six straight sides form a closed two-dimensional boundary.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","A circle is a polygon because its curved boundary is made entirely from straight line segments.","A hexagon is a polygon because its closed boundary consists of straight line segments.","A polygon has straight sides; a circle has a curved boundary.")],quiz:[Q("polygon.q1","polygon.s1","meaning","A polygon is a closed shape made from ___.",["straight line segments","one continuous curve only","separate dots with no boundary"],"straight line segments","The definition requires a closed plane figure bounded by straight lines.","meaning"),Q("polygon.q2","polygon.s1","context","Which figure is a polygon?",["A closed pentagon","An open curved arc","A round ball in three dimensions"],"A closed pentagon","A pentagon is a closed plane shape with straight sides.","context"),Q("polygon.q3","polygon.s1","word-choice","A triangle is the simplest common ____ with three straight sides.",["polygon","polymer","polyp"],"polygon","A triangle is a closed plane figure bounded by segments.","word-choice"),Q("polygon.q4","polygon.s1","meaning","Why is a circle not a polygon?",["Its boundary is curved rather than made of straight sides.","It has exactly five sides.","It is open at one corner."],"Its boundary is curved rather than made of straight sides.","Polygons are bounded by line segments, unlike circles.","meaning")]});
D("polygonal",{etymology:E("Formed from polygon + -al; polygon comes from Greek polygōnon ‘many-angled’, and the suffix -al makes an adjective meaning shaped like or relating to a polygon.",null,"polygon","-al","Etymonline, polygonal (https://www.etymonline.com/word/polygonal)."),contexts:[C("polygonal.s1","數學","The architect chose a polygonal floor plan with eight straight outer walls around the central hall.","建築師選擇多邊形平面配置，以八面筆直外牆環繞中央大廳。","Polygonal means shaped like a polygon.","Polygonal modifies floor plan; with introduces its geometric details.","The plan’s straight sides create a polygon-like outline.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The polygonal pool had a perfectly circular outline with no straight edges or corners.","The polygonal pool had a closed outline made of several straight sides.","Polygonal describes a many-sided straight-edged shape, not a circle with no sides.")],quiz:[Q("polygonal.q1","polygonal.s1","meaning","A polygonal outline has ___.",["several straight sides","only a smooth curved edge","no boundary at all"],"several straight sides","The adjective means shaped like a polygon.","meaning"),Q("polygonal.q2","polygonal.s1","context","Which object has a polygonal shape?",["A stop sign with straight edges","A smooth soap bubble","A round coin"],"A stop sign with straight edges","The stop sign’s boundary is made of line segments.","context"),Q("polygonal.q3","polygonal.s1","word-choice","The sculpture stood on a ____ base with six flat sides.",["polygonal","polygamous","pompous"],"polygonal","The base has a polygon-like outline.","word-choice"),Q("polygonal.q4","polygonal.s1","word-formation","What does -al do in polygonal?",["Forms an adjective meaning relating to or shaped like a polygon","Makes the word mean a single angle","Changes it into a verb meaning draw"],"Forms an adjective meaning relating to or shaped like a polygon","The suffix -al commonly forms adjectives from nouns.","word-formation")]});
D("polymer",{etymology:E("Coined from Greek poly- ‘many’ + meros ‘part’ for a substance built from repeating molecular units; the term was introduced in chemistry for compounds of large molecular weight.","poly","meros","-er","Etymonline, polymer (https://www.etymonline.com/word/polymer)."),contexts:[C("polymer.s1","科學","The chemist tested how heat changed the polymer made from thousands of repeating molecular units.","化學家測試加熱如何改變由數千個重複分子單元構成的聚合物。","A polymer is a substance made of large molecules built from repeating units.","Polymer is the object of tested; made from describes its structure.","Many linked molecular units form one large molecule or material.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","A polymer contains no repeated molecular units and consists only of one isolated atom.","A polymer contains many molecular units linked in repeating chains or networks.","Polymer refers to a large substance built from repeated molecular parts, not a single atom.")],quiz:[Q("polymer.q1","polymer.s1","meaning","A polymer is made from ___.",["many linked repeating molecular units","one unconnected atom only","a single straight line on a map"],"many linked repeating molecular units","Polymers contain large molecules built from repeating parts.","meaning"),Q("polymer.q2","polymer.s1","context","Which material is an example of a polymer?",["A plastic made of long molecular chains","A pure sample of one atom","A triangular drawing"],"A plastic made of long molecular chains","Many plastics are polymers with linked repeating units.","context"),Q("polymer.q3","polymer.s1","word-choice","The lab measured the strength of a biodegradable ____ film.",["polymer","polyp","pond"],"polymer","The film is a material made from large repeating molecules.","word-choice"),Q("polymer.q4","polymer.s1","word-formation","The Greek element poly- in polymer means ___.",["many","water","color"],"many","Poly- means many, referring to the many molecular parts.","word-formation")]});
D("polymerization",{etymology:E("From polymerize + -ation; polymer derives from Greek poly- ‘many’ + meros ‘part’. Polymerization is the process in which many small molecules link to form a polymer.",null,"polymer","-ization","Etymonline, polymerize (https://www.etymonline.com/word/polymerize)."),contexts:[C("polymerization.s1","通用","The manufacturer monitored polymerization as the liquid resin hardened into long chains of linked molecules.","製造商監測聚合反應，看液態樹脂如何硬化成互相連接的長分子鏈。","Polymerization is the joining of many small molecules to form a polymer.","Polymerization is the object of monitored; as describes the chemical change.","Small units bond into larger repeating structures during the reaction.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","During polymerization, a large polymer broke into separate atoms and no small molecules joined together.","During polymerization, small molecules joined to form larger polymer chains.","Polymerization builds polymers by linking many small molecules; breaking them apart is degradation.")],quiz:[Q("polymerization.q1","polymerization.s1","meaning","Polymerization is the process of ___.",["joining small molecules into a polymer","breaking every molecule into atoms","painting a shape in several colors"],"joining small molecules into a polymer","The process forms a polymer from many smaller units.","meaning"),Q("polymerization.q2","polymerization.s1","context","What happens as resin polymerizes?",["Its small molecules link into larger chains.","It turns into a polygon on paper.","It becomes a liquid with no molecular structure."],"Its small molecules link into larger chains.","Polymerization joins monomers into polymer chains.","context"),Q("polymerization.q3","polymerization.s1","word-choice","Heat triggered ____ in the resin, causing it to harden.",["polymerization","poltroonery","polyphony"],"polymerization","The chemical process creates linked polymer molecules.","word-choice"),Q("polymerization.q4","polymerization.s1","meaning","What is the result of polymerization?",["A polymer made from linked repeating units","A single isolated monomer only","A painted sign"],"A polymer made from linked repeating units","The process produces larger molecules from many joined units.","meaning")]});
D("polyp",{etymology:E("From Greek polypous ‘many-footed’, from polys ‘many’ + pous/podos ‘foot’; the word first named a many-limbed sea creature and later a small growth on bodily tissue.","poly","pous","-","Etymonline, polyp (https://www.etymonline.com/word/polyp)."),contexts:[C("polyp.s1","自然","The diver photographed a coral polyp extending its tentacles from a crevice in the reef.","潛水員拍下珊瑚蟲從礁石裂縫伸出觸手的樣子。","A polyp can be a small sea animal fixed to rock or a small growth on body tissue.","Polyp is the object of photographed; extending describes the animal’s action.","The marine polyp stays attached while its tentacles reach into the water.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The doctor identified a polyp in the scan as a large free-swimming whale with fins and a backbone.","The doctor identified a polyp as a small growth on the tissue seen in the scan.","A medical polyp is a small tissue growth, not a large marine mammal.")],quiz:[Q("polyp.q1","polyp.s1","meaning","A polyp may be ___.",["a small tissue growth or a small attached sea animal","a flying bird with feathers","a large inland lake"],"a small tissue growth or a small attached sea animal","The word has medical and marine senses involving a small growth or creature.","meaning"),Q("polyp.q2","polyp.s1","context","A coral polyp is most likely found ___.",["attached to a reef","inside a pine cone","on a school desk"],"attached to a reef","Coral polyps are small sea animals fixed to a surface.","context"),Q("polyp.q3","polyp.s1","word-choice","The scan revealed a small ____ on the lining of the colon.",["polyp","polymer","polygon"],"polyp","A small tissue growth is a medical polyp.","word-choice"),Q("polyp.q4","polyp.s1","meaning","Why does the Greek source of polyp mean “many-footed”?",["The original creature was described by its many appendages.","It refers to many printed colors.","It refers to a group of several spouses."],"The original creature was described by its many appendages.","The name combines Greek elements for many and foot.","meaning")]});
D("polyphony",{etymology:E("From Greek polyphōnos ‘many-voiced’, from polys ‘many’ + phōnē ‘voice, sound’; in music it is the simultaneous combination of independent melodic lines.","poly","phōnē","-y","Etymonline, polyphony (https://www.etymonline.com/word/polyphony)."),contexts:[C("polyphony.s1","音樂","The early choir’s polyphony let the altos and sopranos carry distinct melodies at the same time.","早期合唱團的複調音樂讓女低音和女高音同時演唱不同旋律。","Polyphony is the simultaneous combination of independent melodies.","Polyphony is the subject; let introduces its effect on the singers.","Several melodic lines sound together rather than one melody with simple accompaniment.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The composition had polyphony because every singer repeated exactly the same single melody in unison.","The composition had monophony because every singer repeated the same single melody in unison.","Polyphony combines independent melodic lines; identical unison singing is not polyphonic.")],quiz:[Q("polyphony.q1","polyphony.s1","meaning","Polyphony in music involves ___.",["independent melodies sounding together","one note played once","silence between movements"],"independent melodies sounding together","Polyphony combines several melodic lines simultaneously.","meaning"),Q("polyphony.q2","polyphony.s1","context","Which arrangement shows polyphony?",["Two voices sing different melodies at once.","A soloist sings one melody alone.","An orchestra rests in silence."],"Two voices sing different melodies at once.","Independent simultaneous melodies define polyphony.","context"),Q("polyphony.q3","polyphony.s1","word-choice","The composer layered three independent lines to create ____.",["polyphony","polygamy","pollution"],"polyphony","The simultaneous musical voices form polyphony.","word-choice"),Q("polyphony.q4","polyphony.s1","word-formation","The Greek element phōnē in polyphony means ___.",["voice or sound","marriage","angle"],"voice or sound","Phōnē means voice or sound, as in many-voiced music.","word-formation")]});
D("polytechnic",{etymology:E("From French polytechnique, from Greek poly- ‘many’ + technē ‘art, skill’; the adjective relates to many technical arts, and the noun names a college teaching practical and scientific subjects.","poly","technē","-ic","Etymonline, polytechnic (https://www.etymonline.com/word/polytechnic)."),contexts:[C("polytechnic.s1","教育","She enrolled at a polytechnic to study engineering, design, and applied computing.","她進入理工學院，學習工程、設計和應用計算。","A polytechnic is a college that teaches technical, scientific, and practical subjects.","At a polytechnic gives her institution; to study lists her fields.","The college emphasizes applied and technical education."),C("polytechnic.s2","教育","The school expanded its polytechnic curriculum with practical courses in robotics and materials testing.","學校增加機器人與材料測試等實作課程，擴充理工教育課綱。","Polytechnic as an adjective relates to instruction in many technical arts.","Polytechnic modifies curriculum; with introduces examples of its technical courses.","The courses teach multiple applied technical skills.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The polytechnic offered only classical poetry and no science, technology, or practical subjects.","The polytechnic offered applied courses in engineering, science, and technical skills.","A polytechnic teaches technical, scientific, and practical subjects rather than excluding them.")],quiz:[Q("polytechnic.q1","polytechnic.s1","meaning","A polytechnic is a college focused on ___.",["technical and practical subjects","only religious ceremonies","professional sports"],"technical and practical subjects","Polytechnics teach applied technical and scientific fields.","meaning"),Q("polytechnic.q2","polytechnic.s2","context","Which is a polytechnic course?",["Robotics and machine design","A course only on cloud watching","A class in silent film projection with no technical work"],"Robotics and machine design","The course teaches technical and applied skills.","context"),Q("polytechnic.q3","polytechnic.s1","word-choice","The student chose a ____ for hands-on engineering training.",["polytechnic","polyp","pompous"],"polytechnic","A technical college offers practical engineering education.","word-choice"),Q("polytechnic.q4","polytechnic.s2","meaning","What does polytechnic suggest about a curriculum?",["It covers several technical arts or skills.","It teaches only one ancient language.","It is shaped like a many-sided figure."],"It covers several technical arts or skills.","Poly- means many and technē refers to art or skill.","meaning")]});
D("polytheism",{etymology:E("From Greek polytheos ‘of many gods’, from polys ‘many’ + theos ‘god’; the English noun names a religious system that recognizes or worships multiple gods.","poly","theos","-ism","Etymonline, polytheism (https://www.etymonline.com/word/polytheism)."),contexts:[C("polytheism.s1","宗教","The historian described the ancient city’s polytheism through temples dedicated to several distinct deities.","歷史學家透過供奉多位不同神祇的廟宇，說明古城的多神教信仰。","Polytheism is a religious system with many gods.","Polytheism is the object of described; through introduces supporting evidence.","The city worships multiple deities rather than one god alone.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The essay defined polytheism as belief in exactly one god and the rejection of every other deity.","The essay defined monotheism as belief in one god; polytheism recognizes many gods.","Polytheism means belief in multiple gods; monotheism means belief in one.")],quiz:[Q("polytheism.q1","polytheism.s1","meaning","Polytheism is belief in ___.",["many gods","one god only","no religious beliefs of any kind"],"many gods","The Greek element poly- means many and theos means god.","meaning"),Q("polytheism.q2","polytheism.s1","context","A society with temples to several separate deities practices ___.",["polytheism","polyphony","polymerization"],"polytheism","Worship of several gods is polytheism.","context"),Q("polytheism.q3","polytheism.s1","word-choice","The comparative religion course examined ____ in ancient civilizations.",["polytheism","polygonal","poltroonery"],"polytheism","The course studies systems recognizing many gods.","word-choice"),Q("polytheism.q4","polytheism.s1","meaning","Which belief system is the opposite of polytheism in number of gods?",["Monotheism","Polyphony","Polyandry"],"Monotheism","Monotheism concerns one god, while polytheism concerns many.","meaning")]});
