D("pont",{etymology:E("A South African English term borrowed from Afrikaans pont, ‘ferry’; its deeper history is uncertain, so no unsupported Latin or French root is asserted.",null,"Afrikaans pont (deeper origin uncertain)",null,"Oxford English Dictionary, pont (South African English)."),contexts:[C("pont.s1","交通","The pont carried the farm truck across the river on a cable while the bridge was being repaired.","橋梁維修期間，纜拉渡船用纜繩把農場卡車運過河。","A pont is a flat-bottomed ferry hauled along a rope or cable.","Pont is the subject; across gives its route and on a cable explains its mechanism.","The cable guides or pulls the flat ferry across the water.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The pont crossed the river as a high-speed airplane flying above the water without a cable or boat hull.","The pont crossed the river as a flat ferry pulled along a cable.","A pont is a cable-hauled ferry, not an aircraft.")],quiz:[Q("pont.q1","pont.s1","meaning","A pont is a type of ___.",["cable-hauled ferry","mountain bird","multi-sided shape"],"cable-hauled ferry","The South African term names a flat-bottomed ferry pulled by rope or cable.","meaning"),Q("pont.q2","pont.s1","context","What would a pont carry across a river?",["A vehicle or passengers","A melody through an organ","A seed inside a fruit"],"A vehicle or passengers","A pont is a ferry used to cross water.","context"),Q("pont.q3","pont.s1","word-choice","The farm’s ____ moved the tractor across the river on its cable.",["pont","pompous","pistil"],"pont","The cable-hauled ferry transports the tractor across the river.","word-choice"),Q("pont.q4","pont.s1","meaning","What guides a pont across the water?",["A rope or cable","A runway","A set of flower petals"],"A rope or cable","The ferry is hauled along a line fixed across the river.","meaning")]});
