D("pony",{etymology:E("From Scottish Gaelic pònaidh and French poulenet, diminutive of poulain ‘foal’; the word names a small horse, generally shorter than a standard horse.",null,"poulain","-y","Etymonline, pony (https://www.etymonline.com/word/pony)."),contexts:[C("pony.s1","體育","The children learned to groom the pony before taking turns riding it around the fenced paddock.","孩子們先學著替小馬梳理毛髮，再輪流騎著它繞圍欄馬場一圈。","A pony is a small horse.","Pony is the object of groomed; before sequences grooming and riding.","The animal is a small horse suitable for supervised riding.")],mistakes:[M("meaning","The pony towered over the stable door like a giant draft horse and could not fit through it.","The pony stood low beside the stable door, noticeably smaller than a full-sized horse.","A pony is a small horse, not an unusually huge draft animal.")],quiz:[Q("pony.q1","pony.s1","meaning","A pony is ___.",["a small horse","a large wild cat","a type of tree"],"a small horse","The noun names a horse of small size.","meaning"),Q("pony.q2","pony.s1","context","Which animal might a child ride in a fenced paddock?",["A gentle pony","A wild shark","A stone statue"],"A gentle pony","Ponies are small horses often used for supervised riding.","context"),Q("pony.q3","pony.s1","word-choice","The riding school brought a small ____ for the beginner class.",["pony","polymer","pore"],"pony","The small horse is appropriate for beginner riders.","word-choice"),Q("pony.q4","pony.s1","meaning","How is a pony generally different from a full-sized horse?",["It is smaller.","It lives only underwater.","It has no legs."],"It is smaller.","Size is the defining distinction in the source sense.","meaning")]});
